## SQ-EFX-02 | Magic Resistance I stops Poison I
@group A
@commands `/effect give <bot> creativecommon:magic_resistance 60 0`; `/effect give <bot> minecraft:poison 10 0`; read health over 5 s
@pass Health unchanged, no hurt flash
@fails `MagicResistanceEffect.onAttack`: `EffectTickContext` not set (MobEffectTickContextMixin) or config `[magic_resistance] negatedEffectTicks`
@reviewed 2026-11-16
@from batches/r1031/a1_effects.qb
# perfBot bots are invulnerable (Bots.java setInvulnerable): damage reads use a NoAI pillager "qp" on Normal
# (zombies are undead: no Poison). Pillager max health 24.
# self-contained since r1118 (judge-6, 2026-11-18): bot spawn so the chunk entity-ticks (r1118: no player near, 0 Poison II / Wither damage, horse armor gave no effects)
> execute unless entity qe run pbot spawn qe -50 -60 -50 minecraft:overworld survival
sleep 3
> difficulty normal
> kill @e[type=minecraft:pillager]
> summon minecraft:pillager -46 -60 -46 {NoAI:1b,PersistenceRequired:1b,Tags:["qp"]}
sleep 1
> effect give @e[tag=qp,limit=1] creativecommon:magic_resistance 60 0
> effect give @e[tag=qp,limit=1] minecraft:poison 10 0
> data get entity @e[tag=qp,limit=1] Health
sleep 6
> data get entity @e[tag=qp,limit=1] Health
look the two Health reads are equal (24.0f)
> effect clear @e[tag=qp,limit=1]

